= Introduction

The Industrial Systems Institute of the
Haute École d'Ingénierie of Sion developed a smart collar for monkeys. It has been developped to observe the behavior of monkeys in their natural habitat without disturbing them.

A first version has already beed deployed and tested on a real group of monkeys in southern Africa and a second, improved version is currently under development. 

This project aims to establish the fundations for an automated testbench for the smart collar. The testbench should first, allow developpers to run automated tests directly on the hardware in their CI pipeline and second, enable go/no-go tests at the end of the production line to validate that the hardware is functioning as expected and ready to be deployed on the field.

